+## Local iPad M5 optimization port
+
+The local port follows [aksmith-git/nxnative pub/oot-ipad-m5](https://github.com/aksmith-git/nxnative/tree/4b2d73c84d9e2cf99e1b9979de774201625840ba), keeping its NDSR network. `upscaler_replace off` removes the replacement control and prevents saved overrides from replacing it. The earlier custom standard scaler and VR MetalFX replacement are removed. Frame rate now offers the game's own pacing (`0`) as well as 30 and 60, so `fps_real` can be used without an environment file. Defaults remain 60, with late-frame holding off and present snapshots on, as in the source branch.
+
+The shader port includes NDSR gather / matrix reuse, float atomic reductions and cached pool-mark reads. Grouped atomic reductions were corrected during integration: all active lanes execute each collective with nonmatching values masked to zero, rather than reducing inside a divergent group. Synthetic GPU regression tests compare uniform, grouped, divergent and threadgroup sums with the original kernels.
+
+The modern upstream already includes the NDSR gather footprint, HMMA matrix reuse, cached pool-mark reads and every old iPad pipeline seed. Its mesh ABI, cumulative visibility queries and LRU texture owner supersede the old experimental grass pre-pass, segment feedback and fixed ghost ring. Those obsolete paths are not transplanted. `DM_NVN_GHOST` now adjusts the idle LRU cache target while retaining recently used entries. Fixed-resolution overlays remain available through `scripts/oot_res_overlay.py`. Whole-game image quality and iPhone/iPad frame time remain unvalidated on this rebase.
+
 ## Dynamic resolution
 
 - The controller (v131072; found by fingerprint, so the addresses are only for reading): the parameters are `game__gfx__DynamicResolutionParam` (`LoadThreshold`, `ReduceCounterMax`, `IncreaseCounterMax`, and a list of levels, each a `ResolutionReduceScale` and a `Priority`). Once a frame the update (`main+0x805aa0`) reads the frame's GPU time, subtracts what its cost model predicts at the current size and keeps the trend of that residual. The level function (`main+0x8065e0`) adds the residual to the model's cost at each level and returns the best level under the threshold: 0, the full 1536x864, when the current size fits. The update moves down after `ReduceCounterMax` frames that ask for it and back up after `IncreaseCounterMax`. Scripted `GPULoad` hints from event data (`main+0x31c3de0`) and `OneshotSetDynamicResolutionLoadThreshold` adjust it in cutscenes.
@@ -280,3 +291,9 @@ Its 37 kernels that correct samples, NDSR's network among them, gave about 0.25
 - [dav1d decoded one frame at a time](../../../docs/reference/movies.md#dav1d-decoded-one-frame-at-a-time): resolved, the title movie's heavy packets on an M2 Pro; and the drain that must go to its end.
 - [`devicectl` copies a large RomFS image through the Mac's memory](../../../docs/reference/packing.md#devicectl-copies-a-large-romfs-image-through-the-macs-memory): the 26.2 GB image's pushes to an iPad filled a 16 GB Mac's swap and failed; now sent over AFC.
 - [`devicectl`'s `--remove-existing-content` empties the app's whole container](../../../docs/reference/packing.md#devicectls---remove-existing-content-empties-the-apps-whole-container): the first complete copy of the image, deleted by the DLC step after it.
+
+## Optional BC mip memory reduction
+
+The game settings expose **Reduce BC texture memory**, **Minimum texture width** and **Minimum texture height**. The default is on for iOS and off for Mac, with independent 512-pixel thresholds. Only read-only BC textures with multiple mip levels are eligible. Both original dimensions must meet their thresholds. Sampling then starts at mip1, reducing host texture memory at the cost of fine detail. The guest layout stays unchanged. Copies, image writes, render targets and explicit GPU readbacks restore every level, and later uploads keep that full allocation. Restart after changing the settings. `DM_NVN_BC_MIP_SKIP=0` disables it, `=1` enables it, and `DM_NVN_BC_MIP_MIN_WIDTH` / `DM_NVN_BC_MIP_MIN_HEIGHT` set the limits. Older numeric switch values remain accepted as a common threshold.
+
+Validation: `make -C dm/gfx/tests GAME=0400486024DEC000 check_t_bc_mip_skip` exercises uploads, sampled views, alias promotion and copies with native BC and CPU-decoded textures under Metal validation. Device gameplay remains to be checked.
